# Defend the Rider, first mode: "Target permanent you control gains hexproof and indestructible until end of turn." On
# turn 3 Bot2's Ornithopter is refused (the refusal) beside Bot1's own (the positive control); the two keywords are on
# Bot1's Ornithopter that turn and gone on turn 5 (CR 611.2a, 514.2). Bot2's is untouched.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Plains x5
Defend the Rider
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Defend the Rider.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Target permanent you control gains hexproof and indestructible until end of turn.)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Hexproof; Indestructible
[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Graveyard = Defend the Rider
